      "title": "tipc: fix padding after bearer instance string.",
      "message": "tipc: fix padding after bearer instance string.\n\nPresumably if the length of the string is a multiple of 4, it needs zero\nbyts of padding to put the next item on a 4-byte boundary.  This means\nthat (4 - (length % 4)) is not the right formula - a check for whether\nthere's any padding must be done first.\n",
      "author_name": "Guy Harris",
      "author_email": "gharris@sonic.net",
      "authored_date": "2024-04-21T18:19:42.000-07:00",
      "committer_name": "Guy Harris",
